extends RefCounted

## Shared Medieval rules plus only the selected difficulty's mechanics.
const COMMON: String = "CONTROLS\n• Spectator mode beside difficulty launches four AI armies with no player; use camera controls to watch. Spectator maps mirror tile positions and types across all four quadrants, giving each corner the same objective distances; total tile count still varies. The fast-forward icon cycles 1x → 2x → 4x → 8x → 1x in any Medieval match; every new match starts at 1x.\n• L-click or drag a box to select; click a tile to move or an enemy to focus.\n• R-click drag / Space-drag: pan · Wheel: zoom · A: select all · Esc: pause\n\nCAPTURE & HEAL\n• Only seated warriors capture spades/hearts/eligible bases; more allies capture faster. Any living opponent in the tile pauses all capture progress, including moving or fighting opponents. Progress resumes when uncontested; friendly units do not block each other.\n• Human capture times: 1/2/3/4/5/6+ seated warriors take 12/9/6/4/2/1 seconds. Other races: 16.7 seconds divided by seated warriors.\n• Partial capture progress stays when you leave. Original bases require their original race to be eliminated. Conquered bases can be recaptured while their current owner lives.\n• Each captured enemy base adds 6 capacity; losing it removes that bonus. Spawn speed stays unchanged. Spawns alternate across owned bases in order.\n• Owned spades speed spawning; for demons, owned hearts provide the same spawning boost. Owned hearts and bases heal seated warriors at 1.8 HP/sec; demons heal only at bases, never hearts.\n• Elves heal at 3.6 HP/sec on owned hearts; base healing is unchanged. Elves must be sitting and unattacked for 3 seconds to heal. On every difficulty, enemy elves below 30% HP seek the nearest uncontested owned heart/base without a distance limit, move 30% slower until arrival, and recover to full HP. Retreat travel stops after 15 seconds if no healing tile is reached; the elf then fights for at least 3 seconds before reconsidering. Seated healing is not subject to this travel timeout. Retreat cooldown is 30 seconds from arrival. Healing elves retaliate in place without healing in combat. Threatened tile defenders can randomly fight or retreat if cooldown permits; fighting commits for 3 seconds.\n\nSPAWNING & COMBAT\n• Enemy proximity reactions run every simulation tick on every difficulty, including during movement. Elves attack any moving or stationary enemy within their reach, except during healing recovery when they only retaliate. Demons detect enemies within 3 cells and pursue their chosen target until death. They attack adjacent hostile blockers before resuming the original pursuit. Humans detect within 3 cells or their larger attack reach, stay within the tile where the encounter began, then return and regroup.\n• Orcs spawn twice as fast. All races start with 12 capacity.\n• Orcs gain +1 capacity per two owned spades or hearts. Converted orcs are shown as (+N) and do not consume spawn capacity.\n• Melee warriors surround enemies; upgraded humans and elves can attack from farther away.\n• Ranged attacks (reach above 1 cell): 80% hit chance against stationary targets. Moving targets: compare attacker swings/sec to target movement multiplier; faster/equal/slower gives 70%/50%/30%. Melee: 90% against stationary targets; cannot hit moving targets except elves, who can attack moving enemies at any reach.\n• Engaged orcs on one victim receive +0/+1/+2/+3 group punch in stable attacker order: regular orcs deal 2/3/4/5 punch. Converted orcs participate normally; their final punch remains capped at 10.\n• Humans: kills repeat +2 max HP, +2 punch, then +2 attack reach, scaling without a tier cap. Humans hit one target per swing. Fighting on owned tiles grants +1 punch, lasting 3 seconds after leaving.\n• Orc killing blows: 25/50/75/100% conversion chance for 1/2/3/4+ successful hit stacks on the victim in the last 5 seconds; repeated hits by the same orc each add a stack, even above capacity. Converted orcs inherit maximum HP up to 30 and permanent punch up to 10 and spawn at that capped full HP; they use orc group damage, with final punch still capped at 10; reach resets to 1 cell. Temporary bonuses are not inherited.\n• Elves: +1 max HP per kill or damaging assist within 3 seconds. Reach costs 2/3/4 bonus HP per extra cell: +2 HP each to reach 3 cells, then +3 HP each to reach 5 cells, then +4 HP each forever. Owned tiles grant no punch bonus.\n• Demons: +1 punch per kill; 50% chance of +1 punch per qualifying damaging assist within 3 seconds. Demon killers heal 2 HP; assists never heal. Healing is capped at max HP; killers do not also receive assist healing. Enemy demons never retreat to heal. At 8/12/18 punch, movement speed is +20%/+30%/+40%.\n• Assist credit is once per death; HP bonuses do not instantly heal. Bonuses reset on respawn. Eliminate all opponents to win.\n• Assigned units clear enemies on their ordered tile together without chasing outside it. Increased-range units can stop before entering and fire at enemies on that tile as soon as they are in reach. Once clear, stand for 1 second, then sit to capture. After capture, hold and defend until a new command.\n• Melee guards on owned tiles react to enemies within 1 movement cell of the border and may pursue into one directly adjacent tile before returning. Increased-range guards instead detect and fire at enemies within their own attack range while staying on their defending tile. Idle defenders retaliate when hit if their orders permit. Enemy ranged-fire responses apply on every difficulty: humans intercept within max(3 cells, attack reach), keep pursuit inside their encounter tile, and regroup afterward; elf defenders individually choose 50/50 fight or healing retreat (subject to cooldown), holding a fight decision for 3 seconds. Orcs decide individually: pursue, but flee if outnumbered by attackers within 2 tiles or at 20% HP or less, subject to their 10-second cooldown starting only after reaching a tile and sitting, and a 10-second flee window. Demons pursue as a group, then roll once to flee (50%) or keep fighting after losing at least half the original group. Demon proximity pursuit continues until either combatant dies; human interception stays on its encounter tile. Other counter-pursuit has no tile leash; strategic orders do not interrupt these commitments. Explicit player and enemy-planner orders can assign new destinations.\n• Enemy AI units in an invaded owned base attack intruders after their short spawn-standing animation, even during the opening delay. Clear invaders inside the base before engaging border threats or taking other orders; elves may choose healing retreat under their shared recovery rules.\n• Enemy retreat labels stay overhead while active: humans \"Retreat!\", orcs \"Flee!\", elves \"Fallback!\". Fleeing enemy orcs gain 30% movement speed throughout both halves of their flee window. If no capture tile exists in the chosen quadrant, they hold a safe position there instead.\n• Difficulty does not change spawn rates; racial, spade and demon-heart bonuses still apply.\n"
const RULES: Array[String] = [
	"EASY AI\n• Enemy units act individually after the opening idle delay (about 22 seconds), choosing capture, attack or healing orders.\n• No strategic squads. Shared ranged-fire response groups and orc flee cooldowns still apply. Wounded units other than demons can seek owned hearts/bases through the individual AI.\n",
	"NORMAL AI\n• Enemy squads coordinate after an opening delay of about 22 seconds. Decisions occur every 2 seconds, with local enemy awareness (16 movement cells).\n• Groups usually contain 2–4 units; five recruits split into groups of 3 and 2. Groups share capture and attack orders.\n• Humans capture and fight together. Orcs focus one enemy; when locally outnumbered, they flee for 10 seconds, with a 10-second cooldown starting only after reaching a tile and sitting: first 5 seconds toward the quadrant with the fewest enemies, then 5 seconds seeking a capture tile there, prioritising uncontested tiles.\n• Elves retreat below 30% HP to the nearest uncontested owned heart/base, without a distance limit. Retreat movement is 30% slower. They remain committed until arrival and recover to full HP; the 30-second retreat cooldown starts on arrival. At the healing spot they retaliate without chasing, and cannot heal during combat. Threatened tile defenders randomly fight or retreat if cooldown allows; fighting holds for 3 seconds before reconsideration.\n• Demons favour weak nearby victims and compare their group's strength with nearby defenders before attacking.\n",
	"EXPERT AI & BONUSES\n• Enemy AI starts immediately. If no capturable objectives or local enemies remain, groups advance to find surviving opponents rather than waiting indefinitely. Decisions occur every second, with local enemy awareness (16 movement cells).\n• Enemy humans fill groups to 4 and choose capture targets within five capture tiles, preferring no enemies. They commit and fight for the chosen tile. If none is visible, they scout locally to discover more tiles instead of waiting at base. Losing half the original mission group gives one 50% retreat chance; a retreat goes to the nearest owned heart/base without a range limit, has a 45-second cooldown and lasts until full HP. \n• Orcs fill groups to 6 and focus one enemy. Locally outnumbered orcs flee for 10 seconds, with a 10-second cooldown starting only after reaching a tile and sitting: first 5 seconds toward the least-enemy quadrant, then 5 seconds seeking a capture tile there, prioritising uncontested tiles.\n• Enemy elves gain +2 maximum HP per kill or damaging assist (player elves remain +1). All Expert demons gain +2 punch per kill and have a 50% chance of +1 punch per qualifying damaging assist within 3 seconds. Movement speed increases by 5% per complete 2 bonus punch: 7/9/11 total punch gives +5%/+10%/+15%, continuing without the old tier cap.\n• Elves form groups of up to 4 core units; elves with unlocked range may join full groups. Groups prefer separated destinations.\n• Elf priority: heal → protect wounded allies within 10 movement cells → capture → group attacks.\n• Elves use the same retreat rules as every difficulty: below 30% HP, nearest uncontested owned heart/base at any distance, 30% slower during travel, full recovery, and a 30-second cooldown starting on arrival. They retaliate at the healing spot without healing during combat.\n• Demons form groups of up to 4. Priority: defend owned tiles within 10 movement cells → capture → group attacks. They never retreat to heal.\n• Elf retreat cooldown prevents a new retreat, not ongoing recovery. No safe owned healing point means no new retreat. If a destination becomes contested or is lost, an active retreat seeks another safe healing tile and remains committed. Distance is Manhattan distance to the nearest cell on the healing tile.\n"
]
const TOOLTIPS: Array[String] = [
	"Easy: individual enemy decisions with an opening delay of about 22 seconds. Clear the ordered tile, stand for 1 second, then capture and defend within one adjacent tile.",
	"Normal: coordinated groups of 2–4, opening delay of about 22 seconds, local awareness, race-specific combat and retreats. Ordered-tile defence is limited to one adjacent tile.",
	"Expert: no opening delay, race-specific group sizes and priorities, nearby healing with cooldowns. Local awareness and standard spawn rates. Ordered-tile defence is limited to one adjacent tile."
]


static func text(difficulty: int) -> String:
	var selected: int = clampi(difficulty, 0, RULES.size() - 1)
	var shared: String = COMMON
	if selected == ClassicSimulation.Difficulty.EXPERT:
		shared = shared.replace("Elves: +1 max HP per kill or damaging assist within 3 seconds.", "Elves: player units gain +1 max HP and enemy AI units gain +2 max HP per kill or damaging assist within 3 seconds.")
		shared = shared.replace("Demons: +1 punch per kill; 50% chance of +1 punch per qualifying damaging assist within 3 seconds.", "Demons: +2 punch per kill; 50% chance of +1 punch per qualifying damaging assist within 3 seconds, for both player and enemy units.")
		shared = shared.replace("At 8/12/18 punch, movement speed is +20%/+30%/+40%.", "Every complete 2 bonus punch adds 5% movement speed (7/9/11 total punch gives +5%/+10%/+15%, and so on).")
	return RULES[selected] + "\n" + shared


static func tooltip(difficulty: int) -> String:
	return TOOLTIPS[clampi(difficulty, 0, TOOLTIPS.size() - 1)]
